  "title": "5-minute wake-up workout",
  "creator": "NHS",
  "description": "A bedroom routine by physiotherapist Nick Sinfield for the NHS: gentle in-bed stretches held for 3 to 4 breaths, then a few standing power moves (marching, squats, side stretch, forward bend). Meant to be done every morning to ease stiffness and wake you up. Stretch holds are modelled as about 20 seconds each.",
